ir=3D"ltr"><div><div dir=3D"ltr"><div dir=3D"ltr"></div>Hi Faiza, <div>I am=
 writing to contest HR=E2=80=99s and both executives attempting to accuse m=
e of abandonment of employment. I will seek legal counsel due to disagreeme=
nts with multiple aspects of this letter, such as the dates and the fact th=
at I am a protected employee who has provided a work capacity certificate. =
I am currently undergoing medical treatment with an upcoming psychiatric ap=
pointment, which can be confirmed as of last month.</div><div>I fully inten=
d to file both stop harassment and bullying case and employment protection =
case to industrial relations against Human Resources if this continues. I b=
elieve this letter has been issued without proper diligence and due process=
, aiming to avoid overturning liability.</div><div>Currently, the industria=
l relations department has accepted the review, which I seek to overturn th=
e liability factor. This does not mean that I am no longer an employee with=
out an injury that should be denied any leave. Documents have been supplied=
 so leave and payments must be actioned. The breach is with my employer not=
 paying my entitlements yet continue to do so.</div><div>Throughout this pr=
ocess, I have communicated through my doctor and WorkCover, and QLD Health =
has been given updates at every step. However, Human Resources have purpose=
ly delayed and coerced the outcome of the WorkCover claim, with corresponde=
nce twice exceeding a month over the 5 days allowed.</div><div>Please let m=
e know if you would like an update on my medical treatment. However, I cann=
ot follow the directive in this letter as it breaches the Fair Work Act, In=
dustrial Relations Act, Human Rights, and the EB11 HHS agreement. There are=
 general protections for employees suffering from an injury, and although t=
he review process will seek clarification on liability, WorkCover has given=
 QLD Health an outcome letter and correspondence acknowledging a =E2=80=98p=
ersonal injury=E2=80=99 while making no accommodations for me and disregard=
ing any injury or work capacity certificates supplied to Human Resources. I=
 find this letter disrespectful to my dignity and health.</div><div>I also =
find it extremely offensive and inappropriate to include the fact that I to=
ok leave when my grandfather died in this letter or in making any decision =
or directive regarding employment abandonment following a communication to =
return to work. This letter is antagonistic and lacks legal justification, =
which would understandably trigger anyone.</div><div>I also request again, =
following many emails to Ms. Taylor, Ms. Reece, Ms. Stibbard, and Amy Mo fr=
om WorkCover, that fatigue pay be issued, referencing the outcome of the Wo=
rkCover notice to be paid overtime when allowing an employee less than 10 h=
ours between shifts. Chloe allowed me only 7 hours, not including travel ti=
me. Not issuing payments and entitlements constitutes wage theft, and I hav=
e already submitted a crime and corruption complaint against QLD Health emp=
loyees.</div><div>Additionally, I formally request that my leave be process=
ed and that HR and executives respect their legal, ethical, and contractual=
 obligations and responsibilities prior to any legal action.</div><div>Than=
k you for your time. Please leave a voicemail when calling, and I will retu=
rn your phone call. I have not received any calls from the contact number p=
rovided here. I have been using WorkCover and my doctor to communicate with=
 my employer, essentially through a third party, to provide updates. As a r=
elevant contact has not been provided to me following my grievances with Ms=
. Reese and Ms. Taylor. I also note the false dates of contact included in =
this letter. I can supply additional evidence in response to this, but it h=
as been advised to Ms Taylor that HR would receive information and updates =
through WorkCover, including a work capacity certificate. Therefore, Ms. Ta=
ylor or HR choosing to ignore communication does not meet the criteria for =
abandonment of employment of an injured employee unable to communicate effe=
ctively.</div><div>I also accept communication via telephone and email, tho=
ugh I prefer email from those who do not seek to antagonize my injury or ca=
use mental or financial harm. If you wish to schedule a time to contact me =
by phone, you can reach me at 0422 438 627.</div><div>Regards,</div>Cory <d=
